  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the file set establishing the dependency graph:\n\n- **next.js \u2192 babel**: real runtime edge. `packages/next/package.json` pins `@babel/core`, `@babel/preset-env`, `@babel/preset-react`, `@babel/preset-typescript`, `@babel/traverse`, `@babel/generator`, etc. under `devDependencies`, but `packages/next/taskfile.js` vendors them via ncc into `next/dist/compiled/babel/*`, which `packages/next/src/build/babel/preset.ts`, `.../babel/loader/get-config.ts`, `.../babel/loader/transform.ts`, and `.../babel/plugins/*` import directly \u2014 this is Next's `next/babel` legacy/custom-`.babelrc` compilation pipeline.\n- **next.js \u2192 webpack**: same vendoring pattern (`webpack: 5.86.0` devDependency \u2192 `next/dist/compiled/webpack/webpack`, imported throughout `packages/next/src/build/webpack-config.ts` etc.) \u2014 independent edge, not mediated by babel.\n- **webpack \u2192 babel**: no real edge. `@babel/core`/`@babel/preset-react`/`babel-loader` appear only in webpack's own `devDependencies` (test fixtures, examples); webpack's shipped `dependencies` use `acorn`/`acorn-import-assertions` for parsing, and no `@babel/*` import exists anywhere in webpack's `lib/` source.",
